r subtype restricts it so that the full noun phrase denotes one identifiable disease in context, THEN label the entire noun phrase as **SpecificDisease**, treating the premodifier as narrowing the referent rather than as evidence of a superordinate class. A differential or contrastive frame (e.g., \"causes of X\") does not by itself override this restriction.\n  - **Negative Constraint:** Do NOT apply this rule when (a) the head noun is unmodified or is modified only by terms of degree, duration, or evaluation that do not fix a single entity; (b) the premodifier is part of a lexicalized phenotype or category name whose modifier does not narrow the referent to one condition, in which case **DiseaseClass** remains correct; (c) the phrase denotes a family or set of entities, such as plurals, enumerations, or \"types of X\"; or (d) the mention is already a named or eponymous disease, which is SpecificDisease without any further restriction.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1830, "output_tokens": 1955, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1558}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}